<title>FINLAND: FINNISH MAY EXPORTS THROUGH PORTS FELL 4.0 PCT.</title>
<headline>FINNISH MAY EXPORTS THROUGH PORTS FELL 4.0 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish exports through ports</p>
<p>fell 4.0 percent year-on-year in May to 3.17 million tonnes, the</p>
<p>Board of Navigation said in a statement on Monday.</p>
<p>In January-May, exports through ports rose 12.0 percent</p>
<p>year-on-year to 15.22 million tonnes.</p>
<p>May imports through ports fell 0.5 percent to 3.20 million</p>
<p>tonnes but January-May imports were 7.3 percent higher than in</p>
<p>the year ago period at 14.21 million tonnes, the board said.</p>
<p>Paper exports rose 120,280 tonnes or 18.7 percent</p>
<p>year-on-year to 762,111 tonnes in May and January-May paper</p>
<p>exports rose 19.3 percent to 3.78 million tonnes, it said.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-0-6805 0245, news@reuters.fi</p>
</text>
